	(text "The ring: 11 LEDs around the knob, from about 7 o'clock (1) to 5 o'clock (11),\nlit as a bar and dimmed for dark stages using the driver's PWM.\nThe outputs match Flashover's Gain ring (OUT1-11) and On LED (OUT36),\nso the firmware carries over.  OUT12-35 are unused.\n\nFlashover's driver is kept for the first prototype; a smaller chip\ncan be looked at for production.  The driver runs from +5V so blue or\nwhite LEDs have enough headroom; its I2C inputs accept 3.3V logic.\nThe ring is a cheap place to try the acrylic light-pipe insert\n(Construction Research.docx).  LED color is still to be chosen."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 93.98 119.38 0)
		(effects (font (size 1 1)) (justify left))
		(uuid "9925f02a-36bb-4501-8c0b-67b556b4a4df")
	)
	(rectangle
		(start 195.58 50.8)
		(end 248.92 86.36)
		(stroke (width 0) (type dash))
		(fill (type none))
		(uuid "2114936c-0a83-43f4-9eec-b4f904778e90")
	)
